{number: 34}
{title: In the Cross of Christ I Glory}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
In [C] the cross of [G] Christ I [C] glory,
[F] Tow'ring o'er the [C] wrecks of [G] time;
[C] All the light of [F] sacred [C] story
[Am] Gathers [C] round its [G7] head sub-[C] lime.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
When [C] the woes of [G] life o'er-[C] take me,
[F] Hopes deceive, and [C] fears an-[G] noy,
[C] Never shall the [F] cross for-[C] sake me:
[Am] Lo! it [C] glows with [G7] peace and [C] joy.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
When [C] the sun of [G] bliss is [C] beaming
[F] Light and love up-[C] on my [G] way,
[C] From the cross the [F] radiance [C] streaming
[Am] Adds more [C] luster [G7] to the [C] day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Bane [C] and blessing, [G] pain and [C] pleasure,
[F] By the cross are [C] sancti-[G] fied;
[C] Peace is there that [F] knows no [C] measure,
[Am] Joys that [C] through all [G7] time a-[C] bide.
{end_of_verse}
